  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This serves 6 and takes about 3 hours 20 minutes. The thing to watch at the start is the foam: in the first 20 minutes of cooking, grey foam rises to the surface and must be skimmed off regularly or the broth will taste muddy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The heat must stay at a very gentle simmer throughout. A rolling boil makes the meat tough and turns the broth cloudy. Look for a lazy bubble every few seconds, not a vigorous boil."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
